{"title":"Adding two-digit numbers with regrouping","key_idea":"When the ones digits add to 10 or more, you regroup 10 ones as 1 ten and add all tens together.","method":["Write the numbers one above the other, lining up the ones and tens places.","Add the ones: 4 + 3 = 7. Write 7 in the ones place.","Add the tens: 2 + 1 = 3. Write 3 in the tens place.","Read the answer: 37."],"worked_example":{"problem":"32 + 15 = ?","steps":["Line up the digits by place value.","Add the ones: 2 + 5 = 7 in the ones place.","Add the tens: 3 + 1 = 4 in the tens place.","The answer is 47."],"answer":"47"},"key_terms":[{"term":"Ones place","meaning":"the rightmost digit in a number"},{"term":"Tens place","meaning":"the digit to the left of the ones place"},{"term":"Regrouping","meaning":"carrying 10 ones to make 1 ten when the ones add to 10 or more"}],"common_mistakes":["Forgetting to line up the ones and tens places before adding, which leads to a wrong answer.","Adding ones and tens in the wrong order."],"remember":"Always line up ones under ones and tens under tens before you add.","quick_check":[{"q":"Add 21 + 16. What do you get?","a":"37"},{"q":"Add 43 + 22. What do you get?","a":"65"}],"tell_your_child":"First, make sure the ones are in a line and the tens are in a line. Then add the ones first, then add the tens, and you have your answer."}
